From 3f2fb33e47828013c0b8359e415665442f2c82c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raj Bhattacharjea <rbhattacharjea@deepsig.io>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:01:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] phy/cuda: warm up the GPU PRACH detector at construction
 and cache its VkFFT kernel

On a real radio the accelerated build missed slot deadlines right after cell
start and the cell stalled. Reproduced with ru_dummy and bisected to
prach_acceleration_mode alone; an LD_PRELOAD timing trace showed the cost:
the CUDA PRACH detector builds its VkFFT IDFT plan on the first detection,
and initializeVkFFT() compiles the kernel with NVRTC - 15 to 54 ms per pooled
detector instance, on main_pool workers that also carry the DU slot chain.
Five instances warmed up on the first PRACH occasions and every queued
DL_TTI/UL_TTI request was flushed late. Steady state is ~30 us per detection.

Two layers:

- prach_detector_cuda_impl runs one detection on zeroed host input at
  construction for the cell's geometry (long/short format from the DU-low
  translator, rx ports from the factory, zero correlation zone 0 or
  OCUDU_PRACH_WARMUP_ZCZ), so the plan, buffers, kernels and graph exist
  before the first live occasion. The live cell's root sequences differ, so
  the first live detection re-uploads roots and recaptures a graph
  (microseconds). OCUDU_PRACH_ACCELERATION_WARMUP=0 disables it.
- prach_detector.cu keeps the compiled VkFFT image on disk
  (OCUDU_PRACH_VKFFT_CACHE_DIR, default /tmp/ocudu-prach-vkfft; 0/off
  disables), keyed by VkFFT version, CUDA runtime, compute capability, DFT
  size, batch and thread aim, loaded with loadApplicationFromString. A stale
  image costs one recompile and is replaced.

The geometry derivation and backend configuration fill move into
compute_geometry() and make_cuda_config() so the warm-up and the live path
cannot drift apart.

(cherry picked from commit 3c9280d751ff3aa270a695713b40883814830a13)
